why is the score not resetting if the player dies?

response:
The issue with your code is that you're only saving and loading the `SCORE` variable when it changes due to adding points. However, if the player dies (i.e., their health reaches 0), they will lose all their points at once, but the `SCORE` variable won't be updated again until the next time the game starts or the player gains new points.

To fix this, you need to reset the `SCORE` variable whenever the player dies. One way to do this is to add an event listener for the death event in your game object's script. Here's how you can modify your code:

```csharp
using System.Collections;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.UI; // This line enables use of uGUI classes like Text.

public class ScoreCounter : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Header("Static")]
    public static int SCORE { get; set; } = 0;

    private Text uiText;

    private void Start()
    {
        uiText = GetComponent<Text>();
        LoadScore();
    }

    private void Update()
    {
        uiText.text = SCORE.ToString("Score:#,0");
    }

    public void AddScore(int scoreAmount)
    {
        SCORE += scoreAmount;
        SaveScore();
    }

    private void SaveScore()
    {
        PlayerPrefs.SetInt("Score", SCORE);
    }

    private void LoadScore()
    {
        SCORE = PlayerPrefs.GetInt("Score", 0);
    }

    private void OnDeath()
    {
        SCORE = 0; // Reset the score on death
        SaveScore(); // Save the new score
    }
}
```

In this modified version, I've added an `OnDeath()` method to handle the case where the player dies. When the player dies, the `SCORE` variable is reset to 0, and then saved using the `SaveScore()` method. This ensures that the player always has a starting score of 0 when they start a new game.
